<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="3.36" dur="3.24">Hello everybody.</text><text start="7.04" dur="4.479">We had a a big night last night as you</text><text start="9.679" dur="4.241">know. It was a very successful night. I</text><text start="11.519" dur="4.801">think we carried some people across the</text><text start="13.92" dur="4.24">finish line. We&amp;#39;ll see. But that was</text><text start="16.32" dur="5.28">great in Iowa. Now I&amp;#39;m going to Florida</text><text start="18.16" dur="5.199">Fort Myers and we&amp;#39;ll uh I think have a</text><text start="21.6" dur="3.919">we have a tremendous crowd. I can tell</text><text start="23.359" dur="3.92">you they&amp;#39;re lined up miles long, but</text><text start="25.519" dur="4.481">we&amp;#39;ll be there soon. Hi, Steve.</text><text start="27.279" dur="5.601">President Trump. The ceasefire is really</text><text start="30" dur="5.12">good news. Will the first lady be a part</text><text start="32.88" dur="3.76">of the trilateral peace talks that</text><text start="35.12" dur="2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No, but it&amp;#39;s not the worst idea I&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="36.64" dur="1.759">ever heard.</text><text start="37.12" dur="3.68">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Have you</text><text start="38.399" dur="5.761">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; What she wants to do is save children</text><text start="40.8" dur="5.759">and that&amp;#39;s her focus and both sides are</text><text start="44.16" dur="2.719">cooperating with her. So doing a very</text><text start="46.559" dur="1.52">good job.</text><text start="46.879" dur="4.561">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; How did that all come about, Mr.</text><text start="48.079" dur="5.441">President? Uh her initiative and uh they</text><text start="51.44" dur="5.2">contacted both sides and both sides</text><text start="53.52" dur="5.039">wanted to do it. Is there any news now?</text><text start="56.64" dur="3.52">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Any news on a new press secretary that</text><text start="58.559" dur="3.441">you can give us a new press secretary?</text><text start="60.16" dur="3.52">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No, nothing. We&amp;#39;re in no Russia.</text><text start="62" dur="5.04">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Mr. President, you look out that says</text><text start="63.68" dur="4.799">Jared Kushner had access to $2 billion</text><text start="67.04" dur="2.64">from Middle Eastern countries.</text><text start="68.479" dur="2.481">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; It&amp;#39;s a false story.</text><text start="69.68" dur="2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; It&amp;#39;s a false story. You don&amp;#39;t know</text><text start="70.96" dur="3.6">anything about that?</text><text start="71.68" dur="4.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No, it&amp;#39;s a totally false story. Totally</text><text start="74.56" dur="3.12">an incorrect story. It was just fake</text><text start="76.4" dur="3.759">news. It&amp;#39;s amazing.</text><text start="77.68" dur="4.96">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Mr. President, you must know now who</text><text start="80.159" dur="4.561">ordered the Starling access in Ukraine</text><text start="82.64" dur="3.6">to be restricted. Was it?</text><text start="84.72" dur="3.12">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Uh, well, I wouldn&amp;#39;t tell you if I</text><text start="86.24" dur="2.879">didn&amp;#39;t know. I have no idea. But I</text><text start="87.84" dur="3.44">wouldn&amp;#39;t tell you if I did know. Why</text><text start="89.119" dur="4">would I tell you who you is?</text><text start="91.28" dur="4.4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I&amp;#39;m a CNN sir.</text><text start="93.119" dur="7.161">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Why would I tell CNN? Although they did</text><text start="95.68" dur="4.6">do some nice polls on me, I&amp;#39;m not saying</text><text start="100.4" dur="5.759">those polls. I like them more said</text><text start="104.32" dur="4.479">access.</text><text start="106.159" dur="5.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; If there is a problem, I&amp;#39;ll get 20,000</text><text start="108.799" dur="3">non,000</text><text start="112.32" dur="4.24">non. Well, I&amp;#39;m not surprised. It could</text><text start="114.24" dur="4.559">be hundreds of thousand. That was just a</text><text start="116.56" dur="4.72">batch. 20,000</text><text start="118.799" dur="5.441">absolutely fraudulent in California for</text><text start="121.28" dur="5.76">voting. And it could be a 100,000. It</text><text start="124.24" dur="5.2">could be 3, 4, 500,000.</text><text start="127.04" dur="7.44">California is very corrupt in voting. So</text><text start="129.44" dur="7.36">is Minnesota. So are many other states.</text><text start="134.48" dur="4.24">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Early voting. Early voting is at record</text><text start="136.8" dur="4.32">levels in a number of states that are</text><text start="138.72" dur="5.2">critical for Republicans to hold on to</text><text start="141.12" dur="4.32">the Senate. Texas, Ohio, North Carolina.</text><text start="143.92" dur="1.679">Who do you think that early voting is</text><text start="145.44" dur="1.76">going?</text><text start="145.599" dur="4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, nobody knows. I mean, we&amp;#39;ll find</text><text start="147.2" dur="5.2">out. I I think that we&amp;#39;re doing very</text><text start="149.599" dur="4.321">well against Telico. I think we&amp;#39;re doing</text><text start="152.4" dur="3.36">very well. We have the best attorney</text><text start="153.92" dur="3.599">general in the history of Texas running.</text><text start="155.76" dur="3.68">So, I think we&amp;#39;re doing well, but we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="157.519" dur="4.641">going to find out. The numbers are very</text><text start="159.44" dur="4.72">high all over the numbers in like I was</text><text start="162.16" dur="3.76">in Iowa. I saw the enthusiasm last</text><text start="164.16" dur="4.159">night. I think there&amp;#39;s great Republican</text><text start="165.92" dur="5.36">enthusiasm. I really think, you know, I</text><text start="168.319" dur="4.881">keep hearing about different things. You</text><text start="171.28" dur="3.76">you&amp;#39;ve been following me. I&amp;#39;ve been</text><text start="173.2" dur="4.64">you&amp;#39;ve been packed. Every house every</text><text start="175.04" dur="5.6">house is people that can&amp;#39;t get in. Uh</text><text start="177.84" dur="4.479">Fort Buyers, they that&amp;#39;s Florida. They</text><text start="180.64" dur="4.16">say they&amp;#39;ve never seen anything like it.</text><text start="182.319" dur="6.28">So, I mean, if that if that counts, I</text><text start="184.8" dur="3.799">think we&amp;#39;re doing very well.</text><text start="191.68" dur="4.96">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I have not spoken with them.</text><text start="193.76" dur="4.88">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I might I might have to, but I have not.</text><text start="196.64" dur="4.879">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I&amp;#39;ve heard I&amp;#39;ve heard it was fixed, but</text><text start="198.64" dur="4.8">if it&amp;#39;s not, I I&amp;#39;ll stick a message to</text><text start="201.519" dur="3.761">the minority voters that supported you</text><text start="203.44" dur="3.2">so much now that we&amp;#39;re in the midst of</text><text start="205.28" dur="1.84">any message to minority and black</text><text start="206.64" dur="2.08">voters.</text><text start="207.12" dur="3.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I think the minority voters been great</text><text start="208.72" dur="3.92">to me, you know. So, I&amp;#39;ve been great to</text><text start="211.04" dur="5.119">the minority voter. Look what I&amp;#39;ve done</text><text start="212.64" dur="5.84">for for uh as an example with the</text><text start="216.159" dur="4.8">historically black colleges and</text><text start="218.48" dur="4.24">universities. I&amp;#39;ve taken care of them.</text><text start="220.959" dur="4.081">I&amp;#39;ve I&amp;#39;ve been very good to Hispanic</text><text start="222.72" dur="3.84">voters been great to me, but I&amp;#39;ve been</text><text start="225.04" dur="3.279">great to them, too. You know, there&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="226.56" dur="3.679">reason. And I&amp;#39;ve been great to</text><text start="228.319" dur="3.681">Hispanics. That&amp;#39;d be great to blacks.</text><text start="230.239" dur="3.441">That&amp;#39;d be great to pretty much</text><text start="232" dur="4.159">everywhere. It&amp;#39;s a different Republican</text><text start="233.68" dur="5.119">party, but we&amp;#39;re also the the party of</text><text start="236.159" dur="4.08">the worker. It&amp;#39;s a much bigger party</text><text start="238.799" dur="3.921">than it used to be. I mean, if you go</text><text start="240.239" dur="4.961">back 10 years ago before I got on the</text><text start="242.72" dur="4.719">scene, it&amp;#39;s a much more powerful party.</text><text start="245.2" dur="4.72">This is a much bigger, frankly, more</text><text start="247.439" dur="4.72">important party. You&amp;#39;ve been campaigning</text><text start="249.92" dur="4.56">nonstop for the past few weeks. You&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="252.159" dur="4.8">campaign non-stop next week. Who do you</text><text start="254.48" dur="4.879">view right now as the most vulnerable</text><text start="256.959" dur="4.96">Republican Senate candidates?</text><text start="259.359" dur="4.56">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, I wouldn&amp;#39;t want to say that.</text><text start="261.919" dur="3.441">I wouldn&amp;#39;t want to say that, but there</text><text start="263.919" dur="2.881">are a couple that are a little bit</text><text start="265.36" dur="3.6">vulnerable. There are a couple where</text><text start="266.8" dur="3.679">they had a little bad luck over the last</text><text start="268.96" dur="3.679">couple of weeks. Something came out</text><text start="270.479" dur="7.361">about But the Democrats have that done,</text><text start="272.639" dur="6.721">too. I mean, look at you look at Elad in</text><text start="277.84" dur="3.919">Michigan. You take a look at that. I</text><text start="279.36" dur="4.64">mean, he&amp;#39;s had more bad publicity, but</text><text start="281.759" dur="4.401">you know, we&amp;#39;ll see what happens. I do</text><text start="284" dur="4.4">think that some of the networks give too</text><text start="286.16" dur="4.479">much air time to the opponents, if you</text><text start="288.4" dur="4.48">want to know that</text><text start="290.639" dur="4.801">said on Iran, Mike said that there could</text><text start="292.88" dur="4.48">be a stalemate for up to a year and the</text><text start="295.44" dur="3.44">US is preparing for an extended</text><text start="297.36" dur="3.2">conflict. But you keep saying it&amp;#39;s going</text><text start="298.88" dur="4">to</text><text start="300.56" dur="5.12">we could end it very quickly, but Iran</text><text start="302.88" dur="4.48">is a failing nation. We&amp;#39;re taking all</text><text start="305.68" dur="4.079">the oil out that we want. You see that</text><text start="307.36" dur="4">with the homeown straight, our navy and</text><text start="309.759" dur="3.601">we have it blocked up for them but</text><text start="311.36" dur="4.88">nobody else and everybody is taking oil</text><text start="313.36" dur="5.2">out. Uh in fact last week we took more</text><text start="316.24" dur="4.88">oil out than we have ever taken it out</text><text start="318.56" dur="4.079">even before the war. So that and that</text><text start="321.12" dur="4.079">was a big that was the big sticking</text><text start="322.639" dur="4.801">point. So we have that and they have</text><text start="325.199" dur="4.56">inflation. They have no money that you</text><text start="327.44" dur="4.4">know the question is do we want to</text><text start="329.759" dur="4">finish it off or do we let it do we just</text><text start="331.84" dur="4.24">want to let it wither because we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="333.759" dur="4.401">getting everything we want. received. We</text><text start="336.08" dur="4.559">have more oil coming out of the Homo</text><text start="338.16" dur="4.64">Straight today than they did a year ago.</text><text start="340.639" dur="4.161">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Israel, do you think the vice president?</text><text start="342.8" dur="3.36">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; We&amp;#39;re going to vote tomorrow. I think</text><text start="344.8" dur="1.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I think we&amp;#39;re voting tomorrow in</text><text start="346.16" dur="3.12">Florida.</text><text start="346.72" dur="4.16">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; How come doesn&amp;#39;t have a gag order like</text><text start="349.28" dur="2.56">How come Elon Morg doesn&amp;#39;t have a gag</text><text start="350.88" dur="2.879">order like you did?</text><text start="351.84" dur="3.6">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Oh, I love that question.</text><text start="353.759" dur="4.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I love that question. She should have.</text><text start="355.44" dur="5.759">But look, what she did is her whole life</text><text start="358.479" dur="5.761">is a scam as far as I&amp;#39;m concerned.</text><text start="361.199" dur="4.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Her whole life is a total scam. Do you</text><text start="364.24" dur="4.239">think your vice president JD Vance</text><text start="365.919" dur="2.961">should have endorsed Netanyahu just like</text><text start="368.479" dur="2">you did?</text><text start="368.88" dur="2.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I don&amp;#39;t know that he did or did. That&amp;#39;s</text><text start="370.479" dur="2.72">up to him. He didn&amp;#39;t.</text><text start="371.36" dur="3.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I would I would leave that up to him.</text><text start="373.199" dur="3.761">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Mr. President, if there is if there&amp;#39;s</text><text start="375.28" dur="2.88">gridlock for the next two years,</text><text start="376.96" dur="3.28">obviously you don&amp;#39;t want to see that.</text><text start="378.16" dur="3.2">But if there is, would that be bad for</text><text start="380.24" dur="2.959">the US economy?</text><text start="381.36" dur="4.8">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No, it would be probably good because</text><text start="383.199" dur="4.801">we&amp;#39;re taking a tremendous Don&amp;#39;t forget</text><text start="386.16" dur="2.879">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; when you say gridlock, you&amp;#39;re talking</text><text start="388" dur="1.44">about Iran.</text><text start="389.039" dur="1.761">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; That would be</text><text start="389.44" dur="2.879">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I&amp;#39;m talking about gridlock in terms of</text><text start="390.8" dur="3.44">your legislative agenda.</text><text start="392.319" dur="3.6">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Oh, gr that.</text><text start="394.24" dur="4.64">Let&amp;#39;s talk about gridlock with Iran.</text><text start="395.919" dur="4.881">Iran is not able to do much now and we</text><text start="398.88" dur="3.2">could if we wanted to just take all of</text><text start="400.8" dur="3.76">the oil. We could take the whole</text><text start="402.08" dur="4.239">country. We could take all of the oil</text><text start="404.56" dur="4.479">and as you know the hormones trade is</text><text start="406.319" dur="5.201">totally ours and that&amp;#39;s the way we&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="409.039" dur="4.401">keep it. So in that way that would be</text><text start="411.52" dur="4.48">the gridlock&amp;#39;s very interesting because</text><text start="413.44" dur="6.159">they have no money. They have inflation</text><text start="416" dur="6.88">that&amp;#39;s 30% as the highest in the world</text><text start="419.599" dur="4.801">right now. So we&amp;#39;ll see. uh as far as uh</text><text start="422.88" dur="3.759">political gridlock you&amp;#39;re talking about</text><text start="424.4" dur="4.16">if the Republicans didn&amp;#39;t win,</text><text start="426.639" dur="3.361">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; right? Just political gridlock.</text><text start="428.56" dur="3.52">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I think the Republicans are going to</text><text start="430" dur="4.639">win. But if there was, as you call it</text><text start="432.08" dur="4.08">gridlock, what happens is I veto</text><text start="434.639" dur="3.68">everything and then the Democrats come</text><text start="436.16" dur="4.8">and they want to make a deal. So we&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="438.319" dur="4.401">work with you. I mean, if you look</text><text start="440.96" dur="4.56">historically when you have a situation</text><text start="442.72" dur="4.879">where that would happen, if it happens,</text><text start="445.52" dur="3.44">you veto, veto, veto, and then they come</text><text start="447.599" dur="2.641">and they say, &amp;quot;How do we get it done?&amp;quot;</text><text start="448.96" dur="3.04">And you make a deal.</text><text start="450.24" dur="4.16">Now that you know the backstory about</text><text start="452" dur="4.24">Amy Actton and her stepfather and why</text><text start="454.4" dur="5.28">she hasn&amp;#39;t talked to her mom for so</text><text start="456.24" dur="5.84">long, her stepfather was indicted for</text><text start="459.68" dur="4.56">rape. Now that you know all that, sir,</text><text start="462.08" dur="5.679">do you change your mind about the ad?</text><text start="464.24" dur="8.16">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No, it&amp;#39;s a mother speaking badly against</text><text start="467.759" dur="7.361">Amy Atkins and uh to me it&amp;#39;s very easy.</text><text start="472.4" dur="4.56">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; But they haven&amp;#39;t talked for 50 years.</text><text start="475.12" dur="4.24">You know, some if it were my mother</text><text start="476.96" dur="4.079">speaking badly about me, it&amp;#39;d be making</text><text start="479.36" dur="3.92">it the number one story on the news.</text><text start="481.039" dur="4.241">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; But her mother stood by her.</text><text start="483.28" dur="5.359">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; But her mother stood by her after her</text><text start="485.28" dur="4.4">husband had raised for she assaulted.</text><text start="488.639" dur="4.321">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; You don&amp;#39;t know that. You don&amp;#39;t know</text><text start="489.68" dur="5.84">anything. Uh her mother stood by, didn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="492.96" dur="4.16">stand by. Her mother went on television</text><text start="495.52" dur="5.04">and said that the daughter who&amp;#39;s running</text><text start="497.12" dur="6.479">for governor of Ohio is a liar and a bad</text><text start="500.56" dur="4.319">person. And that&amp;#39;s all I know. That</text><text start="503.599" dur="4.081">father was smart.</text><text start="504.879" dur="4.241">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Nobody knows. Nobody knows anything.</text><text start="507.68" dur="4.479">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; But he was part of the president.</text><text start="509.12" dur="5.359">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Can I be honest? You should even You&amp;#39;re</text><text start="512.159" dur="4.721">the press is embarrassing himself.</text><text start="514.479" dur="5.36">You&amp;#39;re trying to take a horrible</text><text start="516.88" dur="5.599">situation for a Democrat and make it</text><text start="519.839" dur="4.481">look better. The mother said really bad</text><text start="522.479" dur="5.201">things about a person that wants to be</text><text start="524.32" dur="5.28">the Democrat governor of Ohio. The</text><text start="527.68" dur="3.839">mother said terrible things. Anybody</text><text start="529.6" dur="4.56">seeing that would say, &amp;quot;No way I&amp;#39;m</text><text start="531.519" dur="5.841">voting for her.&amp;quot; But Mr. Trump, it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="534.16" dur="5.04">very simple. The press is trying so hard</text><text start="537.36" dur="3.84">to nullify it. You know, they called me</text><text start="539.2" dur="3.92">up about it. I said, &amp;quot;Wait a minute. The</text><text start="541.2" dur="4.16">mother said these things. The mother</text><text start="543.12" dur="4.719">looks like she&amp;#39;s totally lucid. She</text><text start="545.36" dur="5.52">looks very smart, actually. And she felt</text><text start="547.839" dur="7.361">she had an obligation to Ohio voters to</text><text start="550.88" dur="7.2">tell them that her daughter is a liar.</text><text start="555.2" dur="4.96">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; President President Silinski says that</text><text start="558.08" dur="3.84">Starling is still not working for</text><text start="560.16" dur="2.239">Ukraine. I haven&amp;#39;t heard that, but I&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="561.92" dur="1.84">look at it.</text><text start="562.399" dur="2.401">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Did you speak with the British prime</text><text start="563.76" dur="2.56">minister today? I did.</text><text start="564.8" dur="1.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Can you tell us what you discussed? Why</text><text start="566.32" dur="2.079">that?</text><text start="566.72" dur="4.88">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; You discussed uh the fact that they&amp;#39;re</text><text start="568.399" dur="5.44">opening up the North Sea oil, and that&amp;#39;s</text><text start="571.6" dur="4.56">going to make uh the UK a very rich</text><text start="573.839" dur="4.321">country. They&amp;#39;re opening up the North</text><text start="576.16" dur="4.88">Sea oil. We discussed I&amp;#39;ve been after</text><text start="578.16" dur="5.04">them to do that for two years. The other</text><text start="581.04" dur="4.479">prime minister, the previous man, Star,</text><text start="583.2" dur="4.16">who&amp;#39;s a very nice man, but he never got</text><text start="585.519" dur="4.401">it done. And this one is getting it.</text><text start="587.36" dur="4.88">Andy is getting it done. And I guess</text><text start="589.92" dur="4.479">it&amp;#39;s against the liberal principle, but</text><text start="592.24" dur="4.48">he knows what&amp;#39;s right. It&amp;#39;s going to</text><text start="594.399" dur="3.12">make it&amp;#39;s going to make the UK a very</text><text start="596.72" dur="2.64">wealthy country.</text><text start="597.519" dur="3.601">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Did you discuss Iran or Ukraine?</text><text start="599.36" dur="4.8">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; We did very very lightly. We mostly</text><text start="601.12" dur="4.719">discussed Aberdine and the North Sea.</text><text start="604.16" dur="4.08">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Can you just talk about the trade talks</text><text start="605.839" dur="3.921">with Mexico? President Shin hope there</text><text start="608.24" dur="4.159">might be a deal before the</text><text start="609.76" dur="4.639">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; We&amp;#39;re very close to a deal with Mexico.</text><text start="612.399" dur="3.281">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; It&amp;#39;ll be a very good deal for hopefully</text><text start="614.399" dur="3.841">them, but it&amp;#39;s going to be a good deal</text><text start="615.68" dur="4.24">for us or we won&amp;#39;t make it. Uh the same</text><text start="618.24" dur="4.32">thing with Canada. Canada is working</text><text start="619.92" dur="4.8">very hard to make a deal with us. And I</text><text start="622.56" dur="3.68">hate to say this, but we have all the</text><text start="624.72" dur="3.04">cards</text><text start="626.24" dur="4.159">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; in both of them.</text><text start="627.76" dur="6.8">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; We have all the cards. Just like I told</text><text start="630.399" dur="7.361">Zalinski, we have all the cards.</text><text start="634.56" dur="5.12">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Romney ad, sir. Republicans like Ashley</text><text start="637.76" dur="3.6">Hson, who you were with last night in</text><text start="639.68" dur="2.96">Iowa, are denouncing the ads.</text><text start="641.36" dur="4.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, they can, but they don&amp;#39;t know the</text><text start="642.64" dur="5.92">fact. Look, this is a mother that went</text><text start="646" dur="4.959">on the air to say that her daughter</text><text start="648.56" dur="4.959">who&amp;#39;s running for governor of the great</text><text start="650.959" dur="4.161">state of Ohio that I won in a record all</text><text start="653.519" dur="3.841">three times. I got the record vote,</text><text start="655.12" dur="4.959">highest vote ever. So, I know it well. I</text><text start="657.36" dur="5.52">love the people. A mother is saying,</text><text start="660.079" dur="4.88">&amp;quot;Don&amp;#39;t put my daughter there because</text><text start="662.88" dur="4.8">she&amp;#39;s a terrible person and she&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="664.959" dur="4.32">liar.&amp;quot; Why shouldn&amp;#39;t somebody do that?</text><text start="667.68" dur="5.04">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; But did the sexual abuse?</text><text start="669.279" dur="4.961">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Let me ask you my mother. Sexual abuse</text><text start="672.72" dur="3.119">allegations make no difference.</text><text start="674.24" dur="2.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Wait, wait, wait, wait. Slow down. Who</text><text start="675.839" dur="2.56">you with? Who you with?</text><text start="676.88" dur="3.12">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I&amp;#39;m with NBC, sir.</text><text start="678.399" dur="3.841">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; One of the worst networks you have.</text><text start="680" dur="2.959">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; But they&amp;#39;re very serious sexual abuse</text><text start="682.24" dur="1.44">allegations.</text><text start="682.959" dur="3.12">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Quiet.</text><text start="683.68" dur="4.32">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; They make no difference to you.</text><text start="686.079" dur="4.561">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Isn&amp;#39;t she a fresh person? You&amp;#39;re a</text><text start="688" dur="5.76">horrible little reporter, aren&amp;#39;t you? If</text><text start="690.64" dur="5.439">my mother said bad things about me, you</text><text start="693.76" dur="4.56">think the Democrats would put it up? I</text><text start="696.079" dur="4.481">think so. But my mother thought I was</text><text start="698.32" dur="4.639">wonderful. Thank you, Mom. My mother</text><text start="700.56" dur="5.2">would never even if she thought them she</text><text start="702.959" dur="6">would never say this is a person a</text><text start="705.76" dur="